        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_236173f98ec84e559becba06bc0deeec",
      "statement": "Audit chain equals mutations: every state change appends exactly one hash-chained audit entry in the same BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction as the mutation, because Store._append_audit runs inside the caller's write cursor and computes seq and prev_hash from the current chain head before inserting; new mutating store methods must preserve this invariant so state never moves without a log line.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/store.py#L196-L261",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:14d4d1dd363ba56d68d6baf2f3959b30e7ae5105e202df3f1325a20a31af67fb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_767e725fe1154b068106327825654609",
      "statement": "The Store opens exactly one SQLite connection per process in WAL mode with isolation_level=None and manual transaction control; all writes serialize behind a single threading.RLock using BEGIN IMMEDIATE with COMMIT on success and automatic ROLLBACK on error, reads share the same connection, and connection pools or async writers are not allowed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/store.py#L158-L208",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:38b24daa341fc4183f5f3513628930405f72ddc810471ee78864118f2a47228b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_12480e49436349dfb62aa9f316ea2873",
      "statement": "Time is injected throughout: all expiry, decay, freshness and checkpoint logic reads an injectable Clock callable (timeutil.system_clock, wrapping time.time, by default) and store/service code never calls time.time() directly, which lets tests drive TTLs, decay and checkpoint cadence deterministically through a MutableClock without real sleeps.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/timeutil.py#L1-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9da5cdbf53e58f8efbef4686ebec680a58b90181484dfbc71af4540503e5c885:"
